</table>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;I,R&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;I,R&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> be the sample set of ground truth image-report pairs in a gold dataset <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\{F_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\{F_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the total list of possible findings in chest X-ray datasets. The set of real Finding-location (FL) pairs extracted by the pre-processing per sample <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=&lt;I_{i},R_{i}&gt;\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=&lt;I_{i},R_{i}&gt;\in D</annotation></semantics></math>
can be denoted by <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FL_{iReal}=\{fl_{ij}\}=\{&lt;f_{ij},l_{ij}&gt;\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FL_{iReal}=\{fl_{ij}\}=\{&lt;f_{ij},l_{ij}&gt;\}</annotation></semantics></math> where:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}=&lt;T_{ij}|N_{ij}|C_{ij}&gt;,l_{ij}=&lt;x_{ij},y_{ij},w_{ij},h_{ij}&gt;." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}=&lt;T_{ij}|N_{ij}|C_{ij}&gt;,l_{ij}=&lt;x_{ij},y_{ij},w_{ij},h_{ij}&gt;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}</annotation></semantics></math> is the jth real finding in report <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the bounding box for the finding <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> in image <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> starting at <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{ij},y_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{ij},y_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> of width <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and height <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> in normalized coordinates ranging from 0 to 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}=\{l_{ij}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}=\{l_{ij}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the list of all normalized locations accumulated across all images of <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> for a finding <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. With normalized coordinates, and since we pick among the valid finding locations, any synthetic location generated for <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> will be valid for some image in the dataset.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The errors found in generated reports are known to include false predictions, incorrect finding locations, omissions, or incorrect severity assessments<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>. We focus on the first two errors so that given a real finding <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> at location <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> for a sample <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we create 3 variants to reflect (a) reversal of polarity (b) relocation of the finding (c) and substitution with appropriate relocation as
<math id="S2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FL_{iFake}=\{&lt;\overline{fl_{ij}},fl_{ik},fl_{mn}&gt;\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FL_{iFake}=\{&lt;\overline{fl_{ij}},fl_{ik},fl_{mn}&gt;\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{fl_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{fl_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reversed finding, <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="fl_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">fl_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is finding <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> relocated to a random new position <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{k}\in L_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{k}\in L_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="fl_{mj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">fl_{mj}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by randomly substituting finding <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m}\not\in F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m}\not\in F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at location <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{n}\in L_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{n}\in L_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> taking care to avoid repeats and contradictions. Table <a href="#S2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 2.1 Training dataset generation ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows synthetic perturbations created from an original finding "yes<math id="S2.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|</annotation></semantics></math>edema" based on the operations above.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Building the FC model</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The end-to-end architecture of the FC model is illustrated in Figure <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2.2 Building the FC model ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We use the encodings of images and FFL text to learn a joint embedding space that is designed to separate the real FFL labels from fake labels using supervised contrastive learning<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. The embeddings from real and fake text-image pairs are then concatenated to learn an inner regression network to predict both the location and veracity of the finding.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vision projection encoder output, and let <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{f_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{f_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the text encodings of findings for each sample <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=(I_{i},F_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=(I_{i},F_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}\in F_{i}=F_{iReal}\cup F_{iFake}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}\in F_{i}=F_{iReal}\cup F_{iFake}</annotation></semantics></math> are the real and fake labels per sample. We define a multi-label cross-modal supervised contrastive loss per sample as:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{SupC_{i}}=\frac{-1}{|F_{iReal}|}\sum_{f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}}log\frac{e^{s_{i}f_{ij}/\tau}}{\sum_{a_{ik}\in F_{iFake}}e^{s_{ia_{ik}}/\tau}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{SupC_{i}}=\frac{-1}{|F_{iReal}|}\sum_{f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}}log\frac{e^{s_{i}f_{ij}/\tau}}{\sum_{a_{ik}\in F_{iFake}}e^{s_{ia_{ik}}/\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{if_{ij}}=z_{i}\cdot z_{f_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{if_{ij}}=z_{i}\cdot z_{f_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the pairwise cosine similarity between image and textual embedding vectors from the real findings <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ia_{ik}}=z_{i}\cdot z_{a_{ik}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ia_{ik}}=z_{i}\cdot z_{a_{ik}}</annotation></semantics></math> is with the fake findings where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ik}\in F_{iFake}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ik}\in F_{iFake}</annotation></semantics></math>. The overall loss is obtained by averaging across all the samples in the batch. Here <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature parameter. This formulation results in a non-diagonal similarity matrix as shown in Figure <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2.2 Building the FC model ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and differs significantly from existing VLM contrastive encoders based on CLIP who all assume a diagonal similarity matrix<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> and are self-supervised. It also differs from supervised contrastive learning which was previously unimodal and used for image classification from augmented version of images treated as positive samples<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. <span id="S2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To our knowledge, the supervised contrastive learning formulation has not been used to develop vision-language encoders with real and fake labels</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, the inner regression network takes the projected joint embeddings <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ijReal}=[z_{i}|z_{f_{ij}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ijReal}=[z_{i}|z_{f_{ij}}]</annotation></semantics></math> of image <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> paired with real finding label <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{ij}\in F_{iReal}</annotation></semantics></math> or fake labels <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ijFake}=[z{i}|z_{a_{ik}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ijFake}=[z{i}|z_{a_{ik}}]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ik}\in F_{iFake}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ik}\in F_{iFake}</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding supervision label <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{g}=&lt;Y_{1g},Y_{2g}&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{g}=&lt;Y_{1g},Y_{2g}&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1g}=&lt;x,y,w,h&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1g}=&lt;x,y,w,h&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{2g}=E=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{2g}=E=1</annotation></semantics></math> for the real finding and 0 otherwise. Using <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{p}=&lt;Y_{1p},Y_{2p}&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{p}=&lt;Y_{1p},Y_{2p}&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> as the prediction from the network, we can express the regression loss per sample as</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{Reg_{i}}=\underbrace{{|{Y_{1p}-Y_{1g}|}}}_{\mathcal{L}_{1}(Y_{1p},Y_{1g})}+\underbrace{\frac{|{Y_{1p}\cap Y_{1g}|}}{|{Y_{1p}\cup Y_{1g}}|}-\frac{|C_{Y_{1p},Y_{1g}}\backslash{Y_{1p}\cap Y_{1g}}|}{|{C_{Y_{1p},Y_{1g}}}|}}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{giou}}(Y_{1p},Y_{1g})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>giou</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{Reg_{i}}=\underbrace{{|{Y_{1p}-Y_{1g}|}}}_{\mathcal{L}_{1}(Y_{1p},Y_{1g})}+\underbrace{\frac{|{Y_{1p}\cap Y_{1g}|}}{|{Y_{1p}\cup Y_{1g}}|}-\frac{|C_{Y_{1p},Y_{1g}}\backslash{Y_{1p}\cap Y_{1g}}|}{|{C_{Y_{1p},Y_{1g}}}|}}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{giou}}(Y_{1p},Y_{1g})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{{|{Y_{1p}-Y_{1g}}|}^{2}}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{mse}}(Y_{1p},Y_{1g})}-\underbrace{[{Y_{2g}\textbf{log}(Y_{2p})}+{(1-Y_{2g})\textbf{log}(1-Y_{2p})}]}_{\mathcal{L}_{BCE}(Y_{2p},Y_{2g})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>mse</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">log</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">log</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{{|{Y_{1p}-Y_{1g}}|}^{2}}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{mse}}(Y_{1p},Y_{1g})}-\underbrace{[{Y_{2g}\textbf{log}(Y_{2p})}+{(1-Y_{2g})\textbf{log}(1-Y_{2p})}]}_{\mathcal{L}_{BCE}(Y_{2p},Y_{2g})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{Y_{1p},Y_{1g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{Y_{1p},Y_{1g}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the convex hull of the bounding boxes defined by <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The loss function reflects the dual attributes being optimized, namely, the location and the veracity of the finding. The L1 loss and generalized IOU loss have previously been used for regression<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>. However, since in our case, the negative findings have bounding box coordinates as <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0,0,0,0&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0,0,0,0&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> which poses a problem for generalized IOU when the prediction error is small. For this reason, and to ensure smooth convergence, we added the mean square penalty. Finally, for the veracity indicator variable <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the binary cross entropy loss.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="S2.F2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.F2.1.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2509.21356v1/revisedfigs/fcmodel.png" id="S2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:499/211;" width="499" height="211" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Illustration of the architecture of our FC model. The real FFL are taken as positive and the fake FFL as negative in the contrastive formulation. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">Implementation details</span>: We used a chest X-ray pre-trained CLIP encoder (151,277,313 parameters)
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> and retained its image encoder (ViT-B/32) and text encoder (masked self-attention Transformer). The joint embedding projection layers of CLIP (768x512 for image and 512x512 for text) were, however, fresh-trained using the new supervised contrastive formulation derived from real-fake labels. The regression network (657,413 parameters) consisted two linear layers, two drop out layers with RELU for intermediate layers and separate sigmoidal functions for producing the output regression vectors as shown in Figure <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2.2 Building the FC model ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. To train this network in an end-to-end fashion, the losses defined in Equations <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Building the FC model ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and  <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Building the FC model ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> were applied at the respective heads shown in Figure <a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2.2 Building the FC model ‣ 2 Method ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The FC model was trained for 100 epochs using the AdamW optimizer on an NVIDIA A100 GPU with 40GB of memory and a batch size of 32. The cosine annealing learning rate scheduler was used with the maximum learning rate of 1e-5 and 50 steps for warm up.</p>
</div>
