<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Error detection using the FC model</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The FFL extracted from an automated report and the image are used by the FC model to predict the veracity of the finding label and its location as shown in Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>b. To quantify the error, we use a phrase-grounded error measure called the FC score<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> which was shown to outperform other evaluation measures such as Radgraph F1, SBERT, and BLEU score. Specifically, we calculate the error detected by FC model as <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RQ(A,P)=1-\mbox{FCScore(A,P)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mtext>FCScore(A,P)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RQ(A,P)=1-\mbox{FCScore(A,P)}</annotation></semantics></math> as :</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RQ(A,P)==1-\frac{1}{2}(\frac{|E_{pj}=1|}{\sum_{E_{pj}\in E_{p}}E_{pj}}+\frac{1}{|L_{p}|}{\sum_{j}\frac{|{L_{Aj}\cap L_{pj}|}}{2|{L_{Aj}\cup L_{pj}}|}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RQ(A,P)==1-\frac{1}{2}(\frac{|E_{pj}=1|}{\sum_{E_{pj}\in E_{p}}E_{pj}}+\frac{1}{|L_{p}|}{\sum_{j}\frac{|{L_{Aj}\cap L_{pj}|}}{2|{L_{Aj}\cup L_{pj}}|}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pj}</annotation></semantics></math> is a predicted veracity for an indicated label <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Aj}\in F_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Aj}\in F_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> in the automated report, and <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{Aj},L_{pj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{Aj},L_{pj}</annotation></semantics></math> are the indicated locations from automated reports and the predicted locations from the FC model respectively computed as shown in Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Phrase-grounded Fact-checking for Automatically Generated Chest X-ray Reports" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>c.</p>
</div>
